16
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:35,800
S&P or Simple Network Time Protocol is a protocol designed to synchronize the clock of devices connected

17
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:36,460
to the internet.

18
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:44,230
The basic operation is as follows The client, or ESP 32, connects to the server using the UDP protocol

19
00:01:44,230 --> 00:01:45,640
on Port 123.

20
00:01:46,390 --> 00:01:51,580
The client transmits the request packet to the server, then the server responds with the timestamp

21
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:52,030
packet.

22
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:55,840
The client can then pass out the current date and time values.

23
00:01:56,500 --> 00:02:02,650
So in general, if the ESP 32 is connected to the internet, it can get the time and date using S&P.

